  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "For a finite group G, let χ1 (G) denote the totality of the degrees of all\nirreducible complex characters of G with allowance for their multiplicities. Suppose\nthat H is a finite group with χ1 (H) = χ1 (G). If G has trivial solvable radical, must\nH also have trivial solvable radical?                                    A. V. Vasil’ev",
